samples,), default=None\n464 |         Sample weights. If None, then samples are equally weighted.\n465 | \n466 |     Returns\n467 |     -------\n468 |     a : float\n469 |         The slope.\n470 | \n471 |     b : float\n472 |         The intercept.\n473 | \n474 |     References\n475 |     ----------\n476 |     Platt, \"Probabilistic Outputs for Support Vector Machines\"\n477 |     \"\"\"\n478 |     df = column_or_1d(df)\n479 |     y = column_or_1d(y)\n480 | \n481 |     F = df  # F follows Platt's notations\n482 | \n483 |     # Bayesian priors (see Platt end of section 2.2)\n484 |     prior0 = float(np.sum(y <= 0))\n485 |     prior1 = y.shape[0] - prior0\n486 |     T = np.zeros(y.shape)\n487 |     T[y > 0] = (prior1 + 1.) / (prior1 + 2.)\n488 |     T[y <= 0] = 1. / (prior0 + 2.)\n489 |     T1 = 1. - T\n490 | \n491 |     def objective(AB):\n492 |         # From Platt (beginning of Section 2.2)\n493 |         P = expit(-(AB[0] * F + AB[1]))\n494 |         loss = -(xlogy(T, P) + xlogy(T1, 1. - P))\n495 |         if sample_weight is not None:\n496 |             return (sample_weight * loss).sum()\n497 |         else:\n498 |             return loss.sum()\n499 | \n500 |     def grad(AB):\n501 |         # gradient of the objective function\n502 |         P = expit(-(AB[0] * F + AB[1]))\n503 |         TEP_minus_T1P = T - P\n504 |         if sample_weight is not None:\n505 |             TEP_minus_T1P *= sample_weight\n506 |         dA = np.dot(TEP_minus_T1P, F)\n507 |         dB = np.sum(TEP_minus_T1P)\n508 |         return np.array([dA, dB])\n509 | \n510 |     AB0 = np.array([0., log((prior0 + 1.) / (prior1 + 1.))])\n511 |     AB_ = fmin_bfgs(objective, AB0, fprime=grad, disp=False)\n512 |     return AB_[0], AB_[1]\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/linear_model/_base.py`.\nFound file `sklearn/linear_model/_bayes.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"hashl