 Update NMF.\"\"\"\n551 |     if beta_loss == 2:\n552 |         # Numerator\n553 |         if XHt is None:\n554 |             XHt = safe_sparse_dot(X, H.T)\n555 |         if update_H:\n556 |             # avoid a copy of XHt, which will be re-computed (update_H=True)\n557 |             numerator = XHt\n558 |         else:\n559 |             # preserve the XHt, which is not re-computed (update_H=False)\n560 |             numerator = XHt.copy()\n561 | \n562 |         # Denominator\n563 |         if HHt is None:\n564 |             HHt = np.dot(H, H.T)\n565 |         denominator = np.dot(W, HHt)\n566 | \n567 |     else:\n568 |         # Numerator\n569 |         # if X is sparse, compute WH only where X is non zero\n570 |         WH_safe_X = _special_sparse_dot(W, H, X)\n571 |         if sp.issparse(X):\n572 |             WH_safe_X_data = WH_safe_X.data\n573 |             X_data = X.data\n574 |         else:\n575 |             WH_safe_X_data = WH_safe_X\n576 |             X_data = X\n577 |             # copy used in the Denominator\n578 |             WH = WH_safe_X.copy()\n579 |             if beta_loss - 1.0 < 0:\n580 |                 WH[WH == 0] = EPSILON\n581 | \n582 |         # to avoid taking a negative power of zero\n583 |         if beta_loss - 2.0 < 0:\n584 |             WH_safe_X_data[WH_safe_X_data == 0] = EPSILON\n585 | \n586 |         if beta_loss == 1:\n587 |             np.divide(X_data, WH_safe_X_data, out=WH_safe_X_data)\n588 |         elif beta_loss == 0:\n589 |             # speeds up computation time\n590 |             # refer to /numpy/numpy/issues/9363\n591 |             WH_safe_X_data **= -1\n592 |             WH_safe_X_data **= 2\n593 |             # element-wise multiplication\n594 |             WH_safe_X_data *= X_data\n595 |         else:\n596 |             WH_safe_X_data **= beta_loss - 2\n597 |             # element-wise multiplication\n598 |             WH_safe_X_data *= X_data\n599 | \n600 |         # here numerator = dot(X * (dot(W, H) ** (beta_loss - 2)), H.T)\n601 |         numerator = safe_sparse_dot(WH_safe_X, H.T)\n602 | \n603 |         # Denominator\n604 |         if beta_loss == 1:\n605 |             if H_sum is None:\n606 |                 H_sum = np.sum(H, axis=1)  # shape(n_components, )\n607 |             denominator = H_sum[np.newaxis, :]\n608 | \n609 |         else:\n610 |             # computation of WHHt = dot(dot(W, H) ** beta_loss - 1, H.T)\n611 |             if sp.issparse(X):\n612 |                 # memory efficient computation\n613 |                 # (compute row by row, avoiding the dense matrix WH)\n614 |                 WHHt = np.empty(W.shape)\n615 |                 for i in range(X.shape[0]):\n616 |                     WHi = np.dot(W[i, :], H)\n617 |                     if beta_loss - 1 < 0:\n618 |                         WHi[WHi == 0] = EPSILON\n619 |                     WHi **= beta_loss - 1\n620 |                     WHHt[i, :] = np.dot(WHi, H.T)\n621 |             else:\n622 |                 WH **= beta_loss - 1\n623 |                 WHHt = np.dot(WH, H.T)\n624 |             denominator = WHHt\n625 | \n626 |     # Add L1 and L2 regularization\n627 |     if l1_reg_W > 0:\n628 |         denominator += l1_reg_W\n629 |     if l2_reg_W > 0:\n630 |         denominator = denominator + l2_reg_W * W\n631 |     denominator[denominator == 0] = EPSILON\n632 | \n633 |     numerator /= denominator\n634 |     delta_W = numerator\n635 | \n636 |     # gamma is in ]0, 1]\n637 |     if gamma != 1:\n638 |         delta_W **= gamma\n639 | \n640 |     return delta_W, H_sum, HHt, XHt\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_fit_multiplicative_update`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n725 | def _fit_multiplicative_update(\n726 |     X,\n727 |     W,\n728 |     H,\n729 |     beta_loss=\"frobenius\",\n730 |     max_iter=200,\n731 |     tol=1e-4,\n732 |     l1_reg_W=0,\n733 |     l1_reg_H=0,\n734 |     l2_reg_W=0,\n735 |     l2_reg_H=0,\n736 |     update_H=True,\n737 |     verbose=0,\n738 | ):\n739 |     \"\"\"Compute Non-negative Matrix Factorization with Multiplicative Update.\n740 | \n741 |     The objective function is _beta_divergence(X, WH) and is minimized with an\n742 |     alternating minimization of W and H. Each minimization is done with a\n743 |     Multiplicative Update.\n744 | \n745 |     Parameters\n746 |     ----------\n747 |     X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n748 |         Constant input matrix.\n749 | \n750 |     W : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n751 |         Initial guess for the solution.\n752 | \n753 |     H : array-like of shape (n_components, n_features)\n754 |         Initial guess for the solution.\n755 | \n756 |     beta_loss : float or {'frobenius', 'kullback-leibler', \\\n757 |             'itakura-saito'}, default='frobenius'\n758 |         String must be in {'frobenius', 'kullback-leibler', 'itakura-saito'}.\n759 |         Beta divergence to be minimized, measuring the distance between X\n760 |         and the dot product WH. Note that values different from 'frobenius'\n761 |         (or 2) and 'kullback-leibler' (or 1) lead to significantly slower\n762 |         fits. Note that for beta_loss <= 0 (or 'itakura-saito'), the input\n763 |         matrix X cannot contain zeros.\n764 | \n765 |     max_iter : int, default=200\n766 |         Number of iterations.\n767 | \n768 |     tol : float, default=1e-4\n769 |         Tolerance of the stopping condition.\n770 | \n771 |     l1_reg_W : float, default=0.\n772 |         L1 regularization parameter for W.\n773 | \n774 |     l1_reg_H : float, default=0.\n775 |         L1 regularization parameter for H.\n776 | \n777 |     l2_reg_W : float, default=0.\n778 |         L2 regularization parameter for W.\n779 | \n780 |     l2_reg_H : float, default=0.\n781 |         L2 regularization parameter for H.\n782 | \n783 |     update_H : bool, default=True\n784 |         Set to True, both W and H will be estimated from initial guesses.\n785 |         Set to False, only W will be estimated.\n786 | \n787 |     verbose : int, default=0\n788 |         The verbosity level.\n789 | \n790 |     Returns\n791 |     -------\n792 |     W : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n793 |         Solution to the non-negative least squares problem.\n794 | \n795 |     H : ndarray of shape (n_components, n_features)\n796 |         Solution to the non-negative least squares problem.\n797 | \n798 |     n_iter : int\n799 |         The number of iterations done by the algorithm.\n800 | \n801 |     References\n802 |     ----------\n803 |     Fevotte, C., & Idier, J. (2011). Algorithms for nonnegative matrix\n804 |     factorization with the beta-divergence. Neural Computation, 23(9).\n805 |     \"\"\"\n806 |     start_time = time.time()\n807 | \n808 |     beta_loss = _beta_loss_to_float(beta_loss)\n809 | \n810 |     # gamma for Maximization-Minimization (MM) algorithm [Fevotte 2011]\n811 |     if beta_loss < 1:\n812 |         gamma = 1.0 / (2.0 - beta_loss)\n813 |     elif beta_loss > 2:\n814 |         gamma = 1.0 / (beta_loss - 1.0)\n815 |     else:\n816 |         gamma = 1.0\n817 | \n818 |     # used for the convergence criterion\n819 |     error_at_init = _beta_divergence(X, W, H, beta_loss, square_root=True)\n820 |     previous_error = error_at_init\n821 | \n822 |     H_sum, HHt, XHt = None, None, None\n823 |     for n_iter in range(1, max_iter + 1):\n824 |         # update W\n825 |         # H_sum, HHt and XHt are saved and reused if not update_H\n826 |         delta_W, H_sum, HHt, XHt = _multiplicative_update_w(\n827 |             X, W, H, beta_loss, l1_reg_W, l2_reg_W, gamma, H_sum, HHt, XHt, update_H\n828 |         )\n829 |         W *= delta_W\n830 | \n831 |         # necessary for stability with beta_loss < 1\n832 |         if beta_loss < 1:\n833 |             W[W < np.finfo(np.float64).eps] = 0.0\n834 | \n835 |         # update H\n836 |         if update_H:\n837 |             delta_H = _multiplicative_update_h(\n838 |                 X, W, H, beta_loss, l1_reg_H, l2_reg_H, gamma\n839 |             )\n840 |             H *= delta_H\n841 | \n842 |             # These values will be recomputed since H changed\n843 |             H_sum, HHt, XHt = None, None, None\n844 | \n845 |             # necessary for stability with beta_loss < 1\n846 |             if beta_loss <= 1:\n847 |                 H[H < np.finfo(np.float64).eps] = 0.0\n848 | \n849 |         # test convergence criterion every 10 iterations\n850 |         if tol > 0 and n_iter % 10 == 0:\n851 |             error = _beta_divergence(X, W, H, beta_loss, square_root=True)\n852 | \n853 |             if verbose:\n854 |                 iter_time = time.time()\n855 |                 print(\n856 |                     \"Epoch %02d reached after %.3f seconds, error: %f\"\n857 |                     % (n_iter, iter_time - start_time, error)\n858 |                 )\n859 | \n860 |             if (previous_error - error) / error_at_init < tol:\n861 |                 break\n862 |             previous_error = error\n863 | \n864 |     # do not print if we have already printed in the convergence test\n865 |     if verbose and (tol == 0 or n_iter % 10 != 0):\n866 |         end_time = time.time()\n867 |         print(\n868 |             \"Epoch %02d reached after %.3f seconds.\" % (n_iter, end_time - start_time)\n869 |         )\n870 | \n871 |     return W, H, n_iter\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_multiplicative_update_h`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n643 | def _multiplicative_update_h(X, W, H, beta_loss, l1_reg_H, l2_reg_H, gamma):\n644 |     \"\"\"Update H in Multiplicative Update NMF.\"\"\"\n645 |     if beta_loss == 2:\n646 |         numerator = safe_sparse_dot(W.T, X)\n647 |         denominator = np.linalg.multi_dot([W.T, W, H])\n648 | \n649 |     else:\n650 |         # Numerator\n651 |         WH_safe_X = _special_sparse_dot(W, H, X)\n652 |         if sp.issparse(X):\n653 |             WH_safe_X_data = WH_safe_X.data\n654 |             X_data = X.data\n655 |         else:\n656 |             WH_safe_X_data = WH_safe_X\n657 |             X_data = X\n658 |             # copy used in the Denominator\n659 |             WH = WH_safe_X.copy()\n660 |             if beta_loss - 1.0 < 0:\n661 |                 WH[WH == 0] = EPSILON\n662 | \n663 |         # to avoid division by zero\n664 |         if beta_loss - 2.0 < 0:\n665 |             WH_safe_X_data[WH_safe_X_data == 0] = EPSILON\n666 | \n667 |         if beta_loss == 1:\n668 |             np.divide(X_data, WH_safe_X_data, out=WH_safe_X_data)\n669 |         elif beta_loss == 0:\n670 |             # speeds up computation time\n671 |             # refer to /numpy/numpy/issues/9363\n672 |             WH_safe_X_data **= -1\n673 |             WH_safe_X_data **= 2\n674 |             # element-wise multiplication\n675 |             WH_safe_X_data *= X_data\n676 |         else:\n677 |             WH_safe_X_data **= beta_loss - 2\n678 |             # element-wise multiplication\n679 |             WH_safe_X_data *= X_data\n680 | \n681 |         # here numerator = dot(W.T, (dot(W, H) ** (beta_loss - 2)) * X)\n682 |         numerator = safe_sparse_dot(W.T, WH_safe_X)\n683 | \n684 |         # Denominator\n685 |         if beta_loss == 1:\n686 |             W_sum = np.sum(W, axis=0)  # shape(n_components, )\n687 |             W_sum[W_sum == 0] = 1.0\n688 |             denominator = W_sum[:, np.newaxis]\n689 | \n690 |         # beta_loss not in (1, 2)\n691 |         else:\n692 |             # computation of WtWH = dot(W.T, dot(W, H) ** beta_loss - 1)\n693 |             if sp.issparse(X):\n694 |                 # memory efficient computation\n695 |                 # (compute column by column, avoiding the dense matrix WH)\n696 |                 WtWH = np.empty(H.shape)\n697 |                 for i in range(X.shape[1]):\n698 |                     WHi = np.dot(W, H[:, i])\n699 |                     if beta_loss - 1 < 0:\n700 |                         WHi[WHi == 0] = EPSILON\n701 |                     WHi **= beta_loss - 1\n702 |                     WtWH[:, i] = np.dot(W.T, WHi)\n703 |             else:\n704 |                 WH **= beta_loss - 1\n705 |                 WtWH = np.dot(W.T, WH)\n706 |             denominator = WtWH\n707 | \n708 |     # Add L1 and L2 regularization\n709 |     if l1_reg_H > 0:\n710 |         denominator += l1_reg_H\n711 |     if l2_reg_H > 0:\n712 |         denominator = denominator + l2_reg_H * H\n713 |     denominator[denominator == 0] = EPSILON\n714 | \n715 |     numerator /= denominator\n716 |     delta_H = numerator\n717 | \n718 |     # gamma is in ]0, 1]\n719 |     if gamma != 1:\n720 |         delta_H **= gamma\n721 | \n722 |     return delta_H\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me also check the beta divergence implementation:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['_beta_divergence', '_beta_loss_to_float']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"_beta_divergence\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_beta_divergence`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `_beta_divergence`.\n```\n 68 | def _beta_divergence(X, W, H, beta, square_root=False):\n 69 |     \"\"\"Compute the beta-divergence of X and dot(W, H).\n 70 | \n 71 |     Parameters\n 72 |     ----------\n 73 |     X : float or array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n 74 | \n 75 |     W : float or array-like of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n 76 | \n 77 |     H : float or array-like of shape (n_components, n_features)\n 78 | \n 79 |     beta : float or {'frobenius', 'kullback-leibler', 'itakura-saito'}\n 80 |         Parameter of the beta-divergence.\n 81 |         If beta == 2, this is half the Frobenius *squared* norm.\n 82 |         If beta == 1, this is the generalized Kullback-Leibler divergence.\n 83 |         If beta == 0, this is the Itakura-Saito divergence.\n 84 |         Else, this is the general beta-divergence.\n 85 | \n 86 |     square_root : bool, default=False\n 87 |         If True, return np.sqrt(2 * res)\n 88 |         For beta == 2, it corresponds to the Frobenius norm.\n 89 | \n 90 |     Returns\n 91 |     -------\n 92 |         res : float\n 93 |             Beta divergence of X and np.dot(X, H).\n 94 |     \"\"\"\n 95 |     beta = _beta_loss_to_float(beta)\n 96 | \n 97 |     # The method can be called with scalars\n 98 |     if not sp.issparse(X):\n 99 |         X = np.atleast_2d(X)\n100 |     W = np.atleast_2d(W)\n101 |     H = np.atleast_2d(H)\n102 | \n103 |     # Frobenius norm\n104 |     if beta == 2:\n105 |         # Avoid the creation of the dense np.dot(W, H) if X is sparse.\n106 |         if sp.issparse(X):\n107 |             norm_X = np.dot(X.data, X.data)\n108 |             norm_WH = trace_dot(np.linalg.multi_dot([W.T, W, H]), H)\n109 |             cross_prod = trace_dot((X * H.T), W)\n110 |             res = (norm_X + norm_WH - 2.0 * cross_prod) / 2.0\n111 |         else:\n112 |             res = squared_norm(X - np.dot(W, H)) / 2.0\n113 | \n114 |         if square_root:\n115 |             return np.sqrt(res * 2)\n116 |         else:\n117 |             return res\n118 | \n119 |     if sp.issparse(X):\n120 |         # compute np.dot(W, H) only where X is nonzero\n121 |         WH_data = _special_sparse_dot(W, H, X).data\n122 |         X_data = X.data\n123 |     else:\n124 |         WH = np.dot(W, H)\n125 |         WH_data = WH.ravel()\n126 |         X_data = X.ravel()\n127 | \n128 |     # do not affect the zeros: here 0 ** (-1) = 0 and not infinity\n129 |     indices = X_data > EPSILON\n130 |     WH_data = WH_data[indices]\n131 |     X_data = X_data[indices]\n132 | \n133 |     # used to avoid division by zero\n134 |     WH_data[WH_data == 0] = EPSILON\n135 | \n136 |     # generalized Kullback-Leibler divergence\n137 |     if beta == 1:\n138 |         # fast and memory efficient computation of np.sum(np.dot(W, H))\n139 |         sum_WH = np.dot(np.sum(W, axis=0), np.sum(H, axis=1))\n140 |         # computes np.sum(X * log(X / WH)) only where X is nonzero\n141 |         div = X_data / WH_data\n142 |         res = np.dot(X_data, np.log(div))\n143 |         # add full np.sum(np.dot(W, H)) - np.sum(X)\n144 |         res += sum_WH - X_data.sum()\n145 | \n146 |     # Itakura-Saito divergence\n147 |     elif beta == 0:\n148 |         div = X_data / WH_data\n149 |         res = np.sum(div) - np.product(X.shape) - np.sum(np.log(div))\n150 | \n151 |     # beta-divergence, beta not in (0, 1, 2)\n152 |     else:\n153 |         if sp.issparse(X):\n154 |             # slow loop, but memory efficient computation of :\n155 |             # np.sum(np.dot(W, H) ** beta)\n156 |             sum_WH_beta = 0\n157 |             for i in range(X.shape[1]):\n158 |                 sum_WH_beta += np.sum(np.dot(W, H[:, i]) ** beta)\n159 | \n160 |         else:\n161 |             sum_WH_beta = np.sum(WH**beta)\n162 | \n163 |         sum_X_WH = np.dot(X_data, WH_data ** (beta - 1))\n164 |         res = (X_data**beta).sum() - beta * sum_X_WH\n165 |         res += sum_WH_beta * (beta - 1)\n166 |         res /= beta * (beta - 1)\n167 | \n168 |     if square_root:\n169 |         return np.sqrt(2 * res)\n170 |     else:\n171 |         return res\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"_beta_loss_to_float\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_beta_loss_to_float`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `_beta_loss_to_float`.\n```\n218 | def _beta_loss_to_float(beta_loss):\n219 |     \"\"\"Convert string beta_loss to float.\"\"\"\n220 |     allowed_beta_loss = {\"frobenius\": 2, \"kullback-leibler\": 1, \"itakura-saito\": 0}\n221 |     if isinstance(beta_loss, str) and beta_loss in allowed_beta_loss:\n222 |         beta_loss = allowed_beta_loss[beta_loss]\n223 | \n224 |     if not isinstance(beta_loss, numbers.Number):\n225 |         raise ValueError(\n226 |             \"Invalid beta_loss parameter: got %r instead of one of %r, or a float.\"\n227 |             % (beta_loss, allowed_beta_loss.keys())\n228 |         )\n229 |     return beta_loss\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, I can now provide the locations that need modification to implement online NMF. Here's the output in the requested format:\n\n```\nsklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py\nline: 120-128\nclass: NMF\nfunction: __init__\n\nsklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py\nline: 725-871\nfunction: _fit_multiplicative_update\n\nsklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py\nline: 537-640\nfunction: _multiplicative_update_w\n\nsklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py\nline: 643-722\nfunction: _multiplicative_update_h\n\nsklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py\nline: 68-171\nfunction: _beta_divergence\n```\n\nThe reason for selecting these locations:\n\n1. `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:NMF.__init__` (lines 120-128):\n   - Need to add new parameter `learning_method` to handle online vs batch mode\n   - Need to add validation for beta loss parameter beyond 2\n   - Existing implementation assumes batch processing\n\n2. `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_fit_multiplicative_update` (lines 725-871):\n   - Core function for multiplicative update NMF\n   - Needs modification to work with online streaming data\n   - Current implementation buffers all data for computation\n\n3. `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_multiplicative_update_w` (lines 537-640):\n   - Handles the W matrix updates\n   - Requires modification to process one batch at a time\n   - Current implementation uses cached computations which won't work online\n\n4. `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_multiplicative_update_h` (lines 643-722):\n   - Handles the H matrix updates\n   - Needs similar modifications to process one batch at a time\n   - Uses cached computations which need to be updated for online case\n\n5. `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:_beta_divergence` (lines 68-171):\n   - Computes the beta-divergence metric\n   - Important for online implementation as it's used to measure convergence\n   - Currently assumes batch processing for computations\n\nThese locations form the core implementation that needs to be modified to support online NMF, particularly focusing on:\n1. Online vs batch processing mode differentiation\n2. Handling of beta loss for non-frobenius cases\n3. Modification of gradient computation functions to operate on one batch at a time\n4. Cache management for online processing\n5. Integration with learning rate scheduling for online learning\n\nThe implementation would need to track running statistics (H_sum, HHt, XHt) only for the current batch rather than maintaining global statistics. This would allow processing of data in batches while maintaining the theoretical guarantees of batch NMF but with reduced memory requirements and online processing capability.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the found locations and analyze their dependencies.\n\nFirst, let me check for any additional NMF-related code that might be relevant:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['OnlineNMF', 'fit_one', 'partial_fit']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant"