ays have the same shape or length.\n455 | \n456 |     Parameters\n457 |     ----------\n458 |     *arrays : list or tuple of input objects.\n459 |         Objects that will be checked for consistent length.\n460 | \n461 |     Examples\n462 |     --------\n463 |     >>> from sklearn.utils.validation import check_consistent_length\n464 |     >>> a = [1, 2, 3]\n465 |     >>> b = [2, 3, 4]\n466 |     >>> check_consistent_length(a, b)\n467 |     \"\"\"\n468 | \n469 |     lengths = [_num_samples(X) for X in arrays if X is not None]\n470 |     uniques = np.unique(lengths)\n471 |     if len(uniques) > 1:\n472 |         raise ValueError(\n473 |             \"Found input variables with inconsistent numbers of samples: %r\"\n474 |             % [int(l) for l in lengths]\n475 |         )\n```\n\nFound function `doc/conftest.py:setup_compose`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n58 | def setup_compose():\n59 |     try:\n60 |         import pandas  # noqa\n61 |     except ImportError:\n62 |         raise SkipTest(\"Skipping compose.rst, pandas not installed\")\n```\n\nFound file `doc/conftest.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `doc/conftest.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"assert_docstring_consistency assert_consistent_docs\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n   1 | \"\"\"\n   2 | The :mod:`sklearn.pls` module implements Partial Least Squares (PLS).\n   3 | \"\"\"\n   4 | \n   5 | # Authors: The scikit-learn developers\n   6 | # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause\n   7 | \n   8 | import warnings\n   9 | from abc import ABCMeta, abstractmethod\n  10 | from numbers import Integral, Real\n  11 | \n  12 | import numpy as np\n  13 | from scipy.linalg import svd\n  14 | \n  15 | from ..base import (\n  16 |     BaseEstimator,\n  17 |     ClassNamePrefixFeaturesOutMix